WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.199 --> 00:00:01.305
- Alright, y'all, welcome back.

00:00:01.305 --> 00:00:03.747
- We've got Taika Waititi here with us.

00:00:03.747 --> 00:00:05.506
(audience claps and cheers)

00:00:05.506 --> 00:00:07.917
You may know our next
guest as Elaine's boss,

00:00:07.917 --> 00:00:10.080
Jay Peterman on Seinfeld,

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:11.722
or as the voice of King Neptune

00:00:11.722 --> 00:00:14.072
on SpongeBob Squarepants, in my household.

00:00:14.072 --> 00:00:16.320
But to every dog lover out there,

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:17.226
he's known as the host

00:00:17.226 --> 00:00:20.010
of The National Dog Show,
which airs tomorrow,

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:21.714
Thanksgiving Day on NBC.

00:00:21.714 --> 00:00:23.940
Please welcome John O'Hurley

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:25.880
along with a couple of
his best friends, y'all.

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:28.232
(crowd cheering)

00:00:28.232 --> 00:00:31.315
(instrumental music)

00:00:35.587 --> 00:00:40.587
(instrument music)
(crowd clapping and cheering)

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:49.517
Oh my Gosh.

00:00:50.375 --> 00:00:52.063
_ [Taika] I'll take him.

00:00:52.063 --> 00:00:52.896
- I want to cuddle with you.

00:00:52.896 --> 00:00:53.729
- [John] You have a job.

00:00:53.729 --> 00:00:54.741
- [Taika Waititi] Okay, great.

00:00:54.741 --> 00:00:55.574
- [Kelly Clarkson] Oh wait,
uou have a job. (laughs)

00:00:55.574 --> 00:00:56.407
- Come here sweetheart.

00:00:56.407 --> 00:00:57.270
- Your character changed.

00:00:57.270 --> 00:00:58.860
- [John O'Hurley] This is Ani and Thyme,

00:00:58.860 --> 00:00:59.693
right here.

00:00:59.693 --> 00:01:02.310
- [Kelly] Aww. Very cute. I
love that you came with dogs.

00:01:02.310 --> 00:01:03.143
Are you a dog person?

00:01:03.143 --> 00:01:03.976
Did you have dogs growing up?

00:01:03.976 --> 00:01:04.980
- [Taika Waititi] Yes, I did. Yep. Yep.

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:06.060
Many dogs.

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:06.893
And a canary.

00:01:06.893 --> 00:01:08.880
- [John O'Hurley] You remember
one of them, in particular?

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:10.110
- [Kelly] Birds are hard in a household.

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:12.259
- Yeah. Rex very original name for my dog.

00:01:12.259 --> 00:01:13.092
(John laughs)

00:01:13.092 --> 00:01:15.998
- [Kelly] He's a Rex. It
was like such amazing name.

00:01:15.998 --> 00:01:16.831
- That's amazing.

00:01:16.831 --> 00:01:18.864
I love when they name him
like old dudes like Bill.

00:01:18.864 --> 00:01:19.697
It's like,

00:01:19.697 --> 00:01:22.290
Well what's your favorite
breed like at the shows?

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:23.970
You've done so many. Over 20 years now.

00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:25.253
- [John] 22 years we've
been doing the show.

00:01:25.253 --> 00:01:26.086
- Yeah.

00:01:26.086 --> 00:01:26.947
- Yeah, usually I kill a show before then.

00:01:26.947 --> 00:01:28.560
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:31.690
My favorite is the Irish setter.

00:01:31.690 --> 00:01:32.523
- [Kelly] Oh.

00:01:32.523 --> 00:01:33.616
- Neck is very erect.

00:01:33.616 --> 00:01:34.449
- [Kelly] Beautiful.

00:01:34.449 --> 00:01:35.370
- Beautiful auburn hair

00:01:35.370 --> 00:01:37.350
on the blue rug as it comes out.

00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:38.730
It always looks like the redhead

00:01:38.730 --> 00:01:40.282
that just walked into the cocktail party.

00:01:40.282 --> 00:01:42.227
- [Kelly Clarkson] Aww.

00:01:42.227 --> 00:01:43.060
- There it is right there you see.

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:43.893
Oh, it's just beautiful.

00:01:43.893 --> 00:01:44.726
- I love it.

00:01:44.726 --> 00:01:45.559
So it's like I said, it's-

00:01:45.559 --> 00:01:47.550
- Not a dog I would own
- [Kelly] It's been over, Why?

00:01:47.550 --> 00:01:48.600
- Well, they're very active.

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:50.700
I mean, you, you need a
lot of property to have a,

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:52.710
I mean they're meant to
be bird dogs or a setter.

00:01:52.710 --> 00:01:54.798
- Yeah, I get that.
- As opposed to you.

00:01:54.798 --> 00:01:56.580
- That's very respectful.

00:01:56.580 --> 00:01:58.320
So wait, over over 20
years, what's like one

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:00.480
of the most memorable
moments at the dog show?

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:01.313
- [Audience] Aww.

00:02:01.313 --> 00:02:02.146
- Well.

00:02:02.146 --> 00:02:04.410
I would say the,

00:02:04.410 --> 00:02:06.270
Oh gosh, a few years back

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:07.770
during the best in show round,

00:02:07.770 --> 00:02:09.420
which is where the top seven dogs

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:10.253
are there,
- [Kelly] Mm-hmm.

00:02:10.253 --> 00:02:11.753
- one of them is gonna
be chosen best in show

00:02:11.753 --> 00:02:15.150
and it's the Great Dane that
happens to be sauntering

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:16.620
by the NBC booth.

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:18.420
Stops in its tracks,

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:19.890
looks me straight in the eye,

00:02:19.890 --> 00:02:22.650
squats down and leaves
what I would refer to

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:25.368
as an editorial comment
right on the floor,

00:02:25.368 --> 00:02:26.201
(audience laughs)

00:02:26.201 --> 00:02:27.207
right there.

00:02:27.207 --> 00:02:29.640
And it stopped the entire show

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:31.170
while the hazmat team

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:32.520
comes out (Taisa laughs)

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:34.080
with the elephant shovels

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:35.670
and has to clean things up.

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:37.074
- The only way
- But that's the only time

00:02:37.074 --> 00:02:37.907
that's happened

00:02:37.907 --> 00:02:38.740
- this story gets

00:02:38.740 --> 00:02:39.686
even better is if that
dog won Best in show.

00:02:39.686 --> 00:02:41.010
(John laughs)

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:43.136
- It it is kind of self
disqualifying, unfortunately.

00:02:43.136 --> 00:02:48.136
- Oh, man. Would've been
funny though. (laughs)

00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:49.501
Do you remember when they
first asked you to host?

00:02:49.501 --> 00:02:51.373
'cause it was such a random thing, right?

00:02:51.373 --> 00:02:52.285
- Well, yes.

00:02:52.285 --> 00:02:53.857
They asked me to host

00:02:53.857 --> 00:02:56.029
and they didn't know what,

00:02:56.029 --> 00:02:57.630
everybody was flying blind

00:02:57.630 --> 00:02:58.650
the first year, including me.

00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:00.390
'cause I had never been to a dog show.

00:03:00.390 --> 00:03:01.980
I didn't know anything about them.

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:03.367
They brought the old English sheep dog

00:03:03.367 --> 00:03:04.334
up to the judge.

00:03:04.334 --> 00:03:05.330
- [Kelly Clarkson] Oh yeah.

00:03:05.330 --> 00:03:07.188
If you don't know what an
old English sheep dog is.

00:03:07.188 --> 00:03:08.570
- Very hairy.

00:03:08.570 --> 00:03:10.170
- Yeah. It's 80 pounds of hair

00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:11.760
and two pounds of actual dog.

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:12.990
- [Kelly Clarkson] Yeah. (audience laughs)

00:03:12.990 --> 00:03:13.823
Which is awesome.

00:03:13.823 --> 00:03:14.656
- They brought it up to the judge,

00:03:14.656 --> 00:03:16.170
who was this elegantly gowned woman.

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:18.000
So she walks around to
the front of the dog

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:19.230
and she starts picking through all

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:20.490
of the hair on the dog's head.

00:03:20.490 --> 00:03:21.802
And I said, David, what is she doing now?

00:03:21.802 --> 00:03:24.063
He says, John, she's
trying to find the eyes

00:03:24.063 --> 00:03:25.530
(audience laughs)

00:03:25.530 --> 00:03:27.750
to gauge the attentiveness of the dog.

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:28.620
I said, really?

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:29.580
Well, she picks through all of

00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:31.020
that hair and she finds only one eye.

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:32.574
She's got the wrong end of the dog.

00:03:32.574 --> 00:03:34.710
(Kelly laughs)

00:03:34.710 --> 00:03:36.750
So you see how far my learning curve was?

00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:38.550
- You said it on air, right?

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:39.383
- Yeah. Oh yes.

00:03:39.383 --> 00:03:40.216
- Oh, I love you so much.

00:03:40.216 --> 00:03:42.030
And it turned into the, you know,

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:43.254
they have the broadcaster's comments

00:03:43.254 --> 00:03:44.112
in the sports section

00:03:44.112 --> 00:03:45.614
- [Kelly Clarkson] Yeah,
that would be the one.

00:03:45.614 --> 00:03:46.447
- and US today.

00:03:46.447 --> 00:03:47.280
That was it.

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:48.113
- [Kelly Clarkson] Yeah.

00:03:48.113 --> 00:03:48.946
- Wrong end of the dog, John O'hurley.

00:03:49.792 --> 00:03:50.699
(Kelly laughs) (audience laughs)

00:03:50.699 --> 00:03:52.410
- Okay. So you have such a great voice,

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:53.243
so have you ever done,

00:03:53.243 --> 00:03:54.270
do you wanna, I think the dog

00:03:54.270 --> 00:03:55.257
wants to go for a walk.

00:03:55.257 --> 00:03:56.090
(audience laughs)

00:03:56.090 --> 00:04:01.090
(John and Kelly laugh) (audience claps)

00:04:01.873 --> 00:04:06.873
(John laughs) (audience laughs and claps)

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:11.673
Oh my God. I love you so much.

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:16.533
She said to the dog,
turn around, come back.

00:04:17.834 --> 00:04:18.667
- [Taika Waititi] Take him back.

00:04:18.667 --> 00:04:19.500
- [Kelly] Oh my God.

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:21.887
- Out for your morning
Constitutional were you?

00:04:21.887 --> 00:04:22.720
(John laughs)

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:24.570
- Physical comedy is the best.

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:26.014
Oh my God, I love you so much.

00:04:26.014 --> 00:04:27.514
- Now, don't you try that.

00:04:27.514 --> 00:04:29.430
(audience laughs)

00:04:29.430 --> 00:04:31.710
- Be sure to watch The
National Dog Show tomorrow

00:04:31.710 --> 00:04:33.600
along with my sister who never misses it.

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:35.283
Thanksgiving day on NBC.

